    {
      "id": "claim_7b1c3aa68413467e93462cc296d17d23",
      "statement": "Tab targeting is per-call and stateless with no hidden selected-tab session state. MCP tool wrappers accept an optional tabId in their schema; the controller's extractTabId reads message.target.tabId (string) and converts to a number once per message; shared page-reader helpers (readActiveTabPage, performActiveTabAction, performActiveTabBatch) prefer the provided tabId over the active-tab query when present and fall back to tabs.query({active:true, currentWindow:true}) when absent; Chrome and Safari adapters forward tabId into these helpers.",
